<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Acer, Mitac hit by profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Acer, Mitac hit by profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan computer giants Acer Inc and Mitac International fell at mid-morning on Tuesday on profit-taking after surging during the electronics sector's recent bull run, brokers said.</p>
<p>With 70 minutes left, Acer was down T$1.5 or 2.78 percent to T$52.5 in active trade.</p>
<p>Mitac had fallen 70 cents or 2.16 percent to T$31.7.</p>
<p>&quot;Many electronics such as Acer have been overbought in recent sessions. I am not surprised that they are hit by profit-taking,&quot; Alex Yang, an analyst of National Securities.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
